Tom: I put them in the recycling bin near my house.
Mia: That''s great. Do you recycle paper too?
Tom: Yes, and I use both sides of every sheet before I recycle it.
Mia: I should do the same. I usually just throw everything away.
Tom: You could start with plastic. Plastic takes hundreds of years to break down.
Mia: Really? Then I''ll bring a reusable bag for shopping from now on.
Tom: Good idea. Small changes like that really help the Earth.', 'Mia 问 Tom 如何处理空瓶和易拉罐;Tom 放进家附近的回收箱,纸张也双面使用后再回收;Mia 平时都扔掉,打算照做;Tom 建议先从塑料开始,因为塑料要数百年才分解;Mia 决定以后购物用可重复使用的袋子;Tom 说这样的小改变真的有助于地球。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Tom do with empty bottles and cans?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He puts them in a recycling bin.","He throws them into the river.","He burns them in the garden.","He keeps them forever."]},{"q":"How does Tom use old paper?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He never uses paper at all.","He uses both sides before recycling it.","He sells it for money.","He eats his lunch on it."]},{"q":"What does Mia usually do with her rubbish?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["She just throws everything away.","She recycles all of it carefully.","She gives it to Tom.","She buries it in the garden."]},{"q":"Why should people be careful with plastic?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It is very expensive to buy.","It takes hundreds of years to break down.","It breaks down in a single day.","It is very good for sea animals."]},{"q":"What will Mia do from now on?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Stop shopping completely.","Use far more plastic bags.","Bring a reusable bag for shopping.","Throw all her bottles away."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U6', 'fltrp');
It describes the dirty air that covers many busy cities.
Long ago, smog was mainly caused by burning coal at home.
Today, most smog comes from traffic and factories.
Smog is dangerous because it can cause serious breathing problems.', 'smog 一词来自 smoke 和 fog;它描述覆盖许多繁忙城市的脏空气;很久以前,雾霾主要由家庭烧煤造成;如今大多数雾霾来自交通和工厂;雾霾很危险,会引起严重的呼吸问题。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where does the word ''smog'' come from?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["From ''sun'' and ''fog''.","From ''smell'' and ''frog''.","From ''smoke'' and ''dog''.","From ''smoke'' and ''fog''."]},{"q":"What does smog describe?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The dirty air over busy cities.","Clean air on a high mountain.","A kind of cloud above the sea.","Fresh air in the countryside."]},{"q":"What mainly caused smog long ago?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Heavy traffic on the roads.","Burning coal at home.","Too many trees in cities.","Strong winds from the sea."]},{"q":"What causes most smog today?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only home coal fires.","Rain and snow.","Traffic and factories.","Cars in the countryside."]},{"q":"Why is smog dangerous?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It makes people very rich.","It cleans the city air.","It cools the whole city down.","It can cause serious breathing problems."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U6', 'fltrp');
Lily: Our teacher said devices in stand-by mode still use power.
Dad: Really? I always thought turning it off was enough.
Lily: No. Electricity keeps leaking from them, even when they look off.
Dad: So we waste power every night without knowing it.
Lily: Yes. If we remove the plug, we save energy and money.
Dad: That makes sense. Let''s unplug the computer too.
Lily: Great. Small habits like this help fight global warming.', '爸爸问 Lily 为什么把电视拔了插头;Lily 说老师讲过待机状态的设备仍在耗电;爸爸原以为关掉就够了;Lily 说即使看起来关了,电仍在漏出;所以每晚都在不知不觉中浪费电;拔掉插头就能省电省钱;爸爸赞同,提议电脑也拔掉;Lily 说这样的小习惯有助于应对全球变暖。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why did Lily unplug the television?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Devices in stand-by mode still use power.","The television was broken.","She wanted to watch films.","It was making too much noise."]},{"q":"What did Dad think was enough?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Unplugging everything at night.","Just turning the television off.","Selling the old television.","Moving it outside the house."]},{"q":"What keeps happening even when a device looks off?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It makes a very loud noise.","It quickly becomes ice-cold.","Electricity keeps leaking from it.","It cleans itself."]},{"q":"What should they do to save energy?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Buy a much bigger television.","Leave everything switched on.","Turn up the heating.","Remove the plug from the socket."]},{"q":"What do small habits like this help do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Help fight global warming.","Waste much more power.","Make the bills higher.","Break the devices faster."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U6', 'fltrp');
A famous film made them believe that all sharks were dangerous.
Because of this fear, fishermen killed millions of sharks.
In fact, sharks harm people only by accident.
Today, more and more people want to protect them from extinction.', '多年来,人们非常害怕鲨鱼;一部著名电影让他们相信所有鲨鱼都很危险;由于这种恐惧,渔民杀死了数百万条鲨鱼;事实上,鲨鱼伤人只是出于意外;如今越来越多的人想要保护它们免于灭绝。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How did people feel about sharks for many years?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["They loved them deeply.","They were very afraid of them.","They knew nothing about them.","They kept them as pets."]},{"q":"What did the famous film make people believe?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["That sharks were friendly.","That sharks could fly.","That all sharks were dangerous.","That sharks were tiny."]},{"q":"What did fishermen do because of this fear?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["They protected the sharks.","They carefully studied the sharks.","They fed the sharks every day.","They killed millions of sharks."]},{"q":"Why do sharks attack people, in fact?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They harm people only by accident.","Because they hate all people.","Because people are their main food.","Because they are never hungry."]},{"q":"What do more people want to do today?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Hunt many more sharks.","Protect sharks from extinction.","Forget about sharks completely.","Sell shark fins for soup."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U6', 'fltrp');
Lin Feng: Of course. It was established in the year 2000 and is very large.
Reporter: What is the biggest problem you face here?
Lin Feng: Large areas of wetland have been damaged by human activity.
Reporter: How does that affect the plants and animals?
Lin Feng: It harms them, and we have also seen more droughts and floods.
Reporter: And what is your team doing to help?
Lin Feng: We protect and restore the land and find sustainable ways to farm.', '记者请林峰介绍这个自然保护区;林峰说它建立于2000年,面积很大;记者问最大的问题是什么;林峰说大片湿地被人类活动破坏;这影响了那里的动植物,还出现了更多旱灾和洪水;记者问团队在做什么;林峰说他们保护并修复土地,寻找可持续的耕作方式。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"When was the reserve established?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["In 1952.","In 1975.","In the year 2000.","Only last year."]},{"q":"What is the biggest problem at the reserve?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Too many visitors every day.","A lack of staff members.","Heavy snow all year round.","Wetland damaged by human activity."]},{"q":"What else has the team seen more of?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["More droughts and floods.","More sunny days.","More tourists.","More new factories."]},{"q":"What is Lin Feng''s team doing to help?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Building many new roads.","Protecting and restoring the land.","Removing all the animals.","Closing the reserve down."]},{"q":"What kind of farming are they looking for?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Cheaper ways to hunt.","Faster ways to cut trees.","Sustainable ways to farm.","New ways to waste water."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U6', 'fltrp');
Try to reduce the amount of energy you use at home.
Turn off the lights when you leave a room.
Unplug any device that you are not using.
These small actions save power and help slow down global warming.', '这里有一个每天帮助地球的小贴士;尽量减少你在家里使用的能源;离开房间时关灯;拔掉任何你不用的设备;这些小行动能省电,并有助于减缓全球变暖。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is this tip meant to help?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["To help you make money.","To help you win a game.","To help you grow taller.","To help the Earth every day."]},{"q":"What should you try to reduce at home?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The amount of energy you use.","The number of books you read.","The amount of homework you do.","The time you spend sleeping."]},{"q":"What should you do when you leave a room?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Open all the windows.","Turn off the lights.","Turn up the heating.","Leave the TV on."]},{"q":"What should you do with devices you are not using?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Buy more of them.","Leave them switched on.","Unplug them.","Sell them at once."]},{"q":"What do these small actions do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Waste a lot of energy.","Make the bills much higher.","Harm the Earth more.","Save power and slow global warming."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U6', 'fltrp');

-- ===== 6) 写作 1篇 =====
DELETE FROM public.junior_writing_prompts WHERE publisher='fltrp' AND volume='required2' AND unit='U6';

We are writing this letter to raise your awareness of the food wasted in our school canteen every day. Each lunchtime, we see large amounts of rice and vegetables thrown away, while many people in the world do not have enough to eat. We are concerned that such waste harms both others and our planet.

In order to improve the situation, we would like to suggest two things. First, only order the food you can finish, and get any leftovers packed to take home. Second, remind your friends to clear their plates.

We hope that you will join us and help make our school a greener place.

Yours,
The Green Club', '【15 分制】A 档(13-15):五要素齐全、组织有条理、语言准确多样;B 档(10-12):要点较全、少量错误;C 档(7-9):要点偏少、句型简单;D 档(0-6):内容不完整、错误多。', '["We are writing this letter to raise your awareness of the food wasted in our canteen.","Each lunchtime, we see large amounts of rice and vegetables thrown away.","Only order the food you can finish, and get any leftovers packed to take home.","We hope that you will join us and help make our school a greener place."]'::jsonb, '[{"wrong":"We see rice and vegetables throwing away.","correct":"We see rice and vegetables thrown away.","note":"rice/vegetables 是被扔的,被动 → -ed 分词 thrown 作补语。"},{"wrong":"Please get the rubbish recycle.","correct":"Please get the rubbish recycled.","note":"get sth done,rubbish 被回收 → -ed 分词 recycled。"},{"wrong":"We are concerned about that the waste is serious.","correct":"We are concerned that the waste is serious.","note":"be concerned that 从句,不加 about。"}]'::jsonb, '【环境倡议信结构】
称呼:Dear Friends,
第1段 唤起关注+问题影响:We are writing to raise your awareness of … We are concerned that …
第2段 两条建议:In order to improve the situation, we would like to suggest … First, … Second, …
第3段 呼吁行动:We hope that you will join us and …
落款:Yours, The Green Club', 2, 'required2', 'U6', 'fltrp');

